title: 'fix: refine ExtrinsicBaseWeight calculation'
doc:
- audience:
  - Runtime Dev
  - Node Dev
  description: |-
    # Description

    This PR refines the calculation of `ExtrinsicBaseWeight` in the `overhead` benchmark by switching from an isolation model to a **"Subtraction" model**.
    Previously, `ExtrinsicBaseWeight` often double-counted the overhead charged by `TransactionExtensions` because the benchmark measured a signed extrinsic without accounting for the extension weights that are already defined elsewhere.
    To resolve this, we now continue to use a standard signed `System::remark` (ensuring we benchmark the real production code path including `Executive::apply_extrinsic`), but we subtract the known weights of the signature verification and included extensions from the final result.

    ## Signature weight

    The cost of verifying a signed extrinsic's signature is now modeled as a static property of the
    signature type, via the new `sp_runtime::traits::SignatureWeight` trait (implemented for
    `MultiSignature` and the primitive `sr25519`/`ed25519`/`ecdsa` signatures). It is recorded during
    signature verification (`Checkable::check`, carried on `ExtrinsicFormat::Signed`) and folded into
    the dispatch weight of signed extrinsics in `GetDispatchInfo::get_dispatch_info`, so it is
    reflected in fees and block-weight accounting without any per-runtime configuration.

    ## Runtime migration note

    When upgrading runtimes to this polkadot-sdk version (including fellowship runtimes), **re-benchmark
    `ExtrinsicBaseWeight`** with `benchmark overhead`, using `--extrinsic-subtract-weight` and passing
    the same `--signature-weight` (and `--extension-weight`, if non-zero) as charged at runtime. If
    `ExtrinsicBaseWeight` is not updated, signed extrinsics will charge signature verification weight
    twice: once via the old inflated base weight and again via `SignatureWeight`.

crates:
- name: frame-benchmarking-cli
  bump: minor
- name: sp-runtime
  bump: major
- name: frame-support
  bump: major
